{:event/actor "seb" :event/at #inst "2026-07-29T17:41:06.676Z" :event/body {:fact/path [:summary] :fact/value "process/roles lives inside the hashed definition (cli_core.clj:271 reads it from load-pinned-process), so authority is pinned at ticket creation. A departed member keeps signed-by authority on every in-flight ticket until each is individually migrated; a new member can approve nothing that already exists; and every hire or departure becomes a definition version bump, so versions stop meaning the rules changed. ADR 0010 describes a different system (time-dependent membership, delegation with expiry, authority chains) that cannot sit on top of this shape. The coupling wants breaking before H3 accumulates tickets: role bindings as a separately-pinned document, or log-carried attestations with process/roles as the default."} :event/parents #{"sha256-70c639fd7cb98e532b49a1c925a8b716cd579331dc5fbbde4fc02b2b988eca12"} :event/ticket #uuid "33d88f7c-5466-48be-a85b-e6ba6e3f2de7" :event/type :fact/assert}